1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,011
GTA 6 isn't just Vice City. It's an

2
00:00:03,011 --> 00:00:06,022
entire state called Leonida, Rockstar's version of Florida,

3
00:00:06,022 --> 00:00:09,033
and Rockstar says it's the largest world they've

4
00:00:09,033 --> 00:00:12,044
ever built. So let's tour every region, and

5
00:00:12,044 --> 00:00:15,056
answer the big question: how big is it

6
00:00:15,056 --> 00:00:15,432
really?

7
00:00:15,682 --> 00:00:18,596
We'll go region by region, from the neon

8
00:00:18,596 --> 00:00:21,510
of Vice City to the swamps, the forgotten

9
00:00:21,510 --> 00:00:24,424
coast and the national park in the north,

10
00:00:24,424 --> 00:00:27,338
plus the districts, landmarks, wildlife, and what's still

11
00:00:27,338 --> 00:00:28,066
only rumour.

12
00:00:28,316 --> 00:00:32,046
First, size. Rockstar hasn't published a square-kilometre figure.

13
00:00:32,046 --> 00:00:35,777
But Aaron Garbut of Rockstar North told Edge

14
00:00:35,777 --> 00:00:39,507
magazine that Leonida's landmass is nearly as large

15
00:00:39,507 --> 00:00:43,237
as GTA 4, GTA 5 and Red Dead

16
00:00:43,237 --> 00:00:44,636
Redemption 2 combined.

17
00:00:44,886 --> 00:00:47,616
He also said it has an order of

18
00:00:47,616 --> 00:00:50,345
magnitude more interiors. That's not a small upgrade.

19
00:00:50,345 --> 00:00:52,734
That's a different kind of open world.

20
00:00:52,984 --> 00:00:55,701
Community mapping projects, which are unofficial, put the

21
00:00:55,701 --> 00:00:58,417
map at roughly one and a half to

22
00:00:58,417 --> 00:01:01,134
two times GTA 5's, with about one point

23
00:01:01,134 --> 00:01:03,850
seven times as a common middle estimate. And

24
00:01:03,850 --> 00:01:06,567
Vice City alone is estimated at two to

25
00:01:06,567 --> 00:01:08,944
three times the footprint of Los Santos.

26
00:01:09,194 --> 00:01:12,875
And those interiors add up. More than seven

27
00:01:12,875 --> 00:01:16,556
hundred enterable interiors have been reported, nightclubs, motels,

28
00:01:16,556 --> 00:01:20,237
restaurants, pawn shops and gun stores, and multi-storey

29
00:01:20,237 --> 00:01:22,538
buildings even have working elevators.

30
00:01:22,788 --> 00:01:25,407
Here's how to find them: on the map,

31
00:01:25,407 --> 00:01:28,026
dark blue buildings have an entrance or an

32
00:01:28,026 --> 00:01:30,645
interior, while light blue buildings are just scenery.

33
00:01:30,645 --> 00:01:33,264
And near an enterable building, the minimap marks

34
00:01:33,264 --> 00:01:35,556
the door with a small white line.

35
00:01:35,806 --> 00:01:39,400
Region one is the heart of it all:

36
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:42,994
Vice City, inspired by Miami. Art deco beachfronts,

37
00:01:42,994 --> 00:01:46,589
nightlife, a glass-tower downtown, canals, and a cruise-heavy

38
00:01:46,589 --> 00:01:47,038
port.

39
00:01:47,288 --> 00:01:50,628
If you played the original Vice City back

40
00:01:50,628 --> 00:01:53,968
in 2002, you'll spot callbacks. Promo material shows

41
00:01:53,968 --> 00:01:57,308
Jason and Lucia outside the Ocean View Hotel,

42
00:01:57,308 --> 00:02:00,648
which was Tommy Vercetti's first safehouse. And Flash

43
00:02:00,648 --> 00:02:03,988
FM, a radio station from the original, is

44
00:02:03,988 --> 00:02:05,240
confirmed to return.

45
00:02:05,490 --> 00:02:08,320
But this Vice City is far bigger and

46
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:11,149
far more modern. Where the original was two

47
00:02:11,149 --> 00:02:13,979
islands of pastel and neon, the new one

48
00:02:13,979 --> 00:02:16,809
is a full city, with social media, influencers

49
00:02:16,809 --> 00:02:19,639
and corporate towers sitting right next to its

50
00:02:19,639 --> 00:02:20,346
rough side.

51
00:02:20,596 --> 00:02:23,714
The city breaks into districts. Ocean Beach, South

52
00:02:23,714 --> 00:02:26,833
Beach, which is the main neon nightlife strip,

53
00:02:26,833 --> 00:02:29,951
and Washington Beach. Vice Beach is a barrier

54
00:02:29,951 --> 00:02:31,900
island linked by a causeway.

55
00:02:32,150 --> 00:02:35,289
Downtown is the financial core. Then there's Little

56
00:02:35,289 --> 00:02:38,428
Cuba, also called Little Havana, and La Perle,

57
00:02:38,428 --> 00:02:41,568
or Little Haiti. Stockyard is the arts district,

58
00:02:41,568 --> 00:02:44,707
covered in murals, and Bayside and the Rialto

59
00:02:44,707 --> 00:02:47,846
Islands are both named on screen in gameplay.

60
00:02:48,096 --> 00:02:51,069
The city also has its own port and

61
00:02:51,069 --> 00:02:54,043
Vice City International Airport, plus a metro station,

62
00:02:54,043 --> 00:02:57,016
a football stadium, a huge amphitheatre, and a

63
00:02:57,016 --> 00:02:59,989
bay observation deck you can use as a

64
00:02:59,989 --> 00:03:01,104
skydiving launch point.

65
00:03:01,354 --> 00:03:04,330
There are tennis courts too, and the Leonida

66
00:03:04,330 --> 00:03:07,306
Penitentiary, which matters more than it sounds, because

67
00:03:07,306 --> 00:03:10,282
it's where Lucia served her time before the

68
00:03:10,282 --> 00:03:11,026
story begins.

69
00:03:11,276 --> 00:03:14,400
Look out for named venues from the gameplay:

70
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:17,525
Megamundo Tower, a corporate headquarters, the Effluvia rooftop

71
00:03:17,525 --> 00:03:20,649
lounge, the Jack of Hearts nightclub, Hank's Waffles,

72
00:03:20,649 --> 00:03:23,773
and the Hotel Dixon on the night beach

73
00:03:23,773 --> 00:03:24,164
strip.

74
00:03:24,414 --> 00:03:27,400
And on the rougher side, the Victory Arms

75
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:30,386
housing project from the opening, Zeke's Gadgets pawn

76
00:03:30,386 --> 00:03:33,372
shop, and the Tisha-Wocka flea market. Vice City

77
00:03:33,372 --> 00:03:35,238
isn't all money and neon.

78
00:03:35,488 --> 00:03:38,374
Region two is the Leonida Keys, based on

79
00:03:38,374 --> 00:03:41,261
the Florida Keys. A chain of tropical islands

80
00:03:41,261 --> 00:03:44,147
linked by bridges, south of the city, and

81
00:03:44,147 --> 00:03:46,312
where the protagonists' starting apartment is.

82
00:03:46,562 --> 00:03:49,303
This is where you'll spend your first hours,

83
00:03:49,303 --> 00:03:52,044
including Key Lento. And it's worth doing the

84
00:03:52,044 --> 00:03:54,785
side content down here early, because coming back

85
00:03:54,785 --> 00:03:56,498
later takes around ten minutes.

86
00:03:56,748 --> 00:04:00,082
The Keys also connect to underwater exploration. The

87
00:04:00,082 --> 00:04:03,416
waters around Leonida have explorable underwater areas, and

88
00:04:03,416 --> 00:04:05,916
that's where treasure diving comes in.

89
00:04:06,166 --> 00:04:10,462
Region three, the Grassrivers, is Rockstar's take on

90
00:04:10,462 --> 00:04:14,758
the Everglades. Mangroves, flooded plains, alligators and airboats.

91
00:04:15,008 --> 00:04:17,840
This is where Leonida feels wild. Alligators are

92
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:20,672
everywhere, and it's also prime territory for chases

93
00:04:20,672 --> 00:04:23,504
that end in the water. Honestly, it might

94
00:04:23,504 --> 00:04:26,336
be the most atmospheric part of the map.

95
00:04:26,586 --> 00:04:28,890
Get yourself an airboat out here. It's the

96
00:04:28,890 --> 00:04:31,194
most fun way to cross the swamp, and

97
00:04:31,194 --> 00:04:33,498
the flooded plains are wide enough that a

98
00:04:33,498 --> 00:04:35,226
car simply won't get you everywhere.

99
00:04:35,476 --> 00:04:38,975
Region four is Port Gellhorn, inspired by Panama

100
00:04:38,975 --> 00:04:42,473
City Beach. Rockstar describes it as a forgotten

101
00:04:42,473 --> 00:04:45,972
coast: cheap motels, dead attractions, a working port

102
00:04:45,972 --> 00:04:47,284
and dirt bikes.

103
00:04:47,534 --> 00:04:49,805
Don't let the rundown look fool you. It's

104
00:04:49,805 --> 00:04:52,076
an important stop for the story, and if

105
00:04:52,076 --> 00:04:54,347
you're into cars, it's where you'll do a

106
00:04:54,347 --> 00:04:55,766
lot of your early business.

107
00:04:56,016 --> 00:04:58,785
Port Gellhorn is also dirt bike territory. Between

108
00:04:58,785 --> 00:05:01,554
the empty lots and the beach, it's a

109
00:05:01,554 --> 00:05:04,324
great place to learn bike handling away from

110
00:05:04,324 --> 00:05:05,016
city traffic.

111
00:05:05,266 --> 00:05:08,848
Region five, Ambrosia, represents central Florida's industry. The

112
00:05:08,848 --> 00:05:12,429
big landmark is the Allied Crystal sugar refinery,

113
00:05:12,429 --> 00:05:16,011
with freight infrastructure around it and a local

114
00:05:16,011 --> 00:05:16,906
biker gang.

115
00:05:17,156 --> 00:05:20,128
Ambrosia is also the name of a county,

116
00:05:20,128 --> 00:05:23,100
which also contains Lake Leonida. It's less glamorous

117
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:26,072
than the coast, which is exactly why it's

118
00:05:26,072 --> 00:05:26,444
interesting.

119
00:05:26,694 --> 00:05:30,227
And region six, Mount Kalaga National Park, on

120
00:05:30,227 --> 00:05:33,760
the northern border. It's inspired by north Florida

121
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:37,292
and Providence Canyon in Georgia. Forests, canyons and

122
00:05:37,292 --> 00:05:37,734
rivers.

123
00:05:37,984 --> 00:05:41,390
This is the outdoors region. Hunting, fishing, kayaking

124
00:05:41,390 --> 00:05:44,796
and off-roading, and it adds its own wildlife,

125
00:05:44,796 --> 00:05:48,203
deer, cougars and foxes, on top of what

126
00:05:48,203 --> 00:05:49,480
you'll find elsewhere.

127
00:05:49,730 --> 00:05:52,718
And remember why fishing matters: calm activities like

128
00:05:52,718 --> 00:05:55,706
fishing raise your Focus stat, and Focus gains

129
00:05:55,706 --> 00:05:58,694
are permanent. So a lazy afternoon at Mount

130
00:05:58,694 --> 00:06:01,682
Kalaga actually makes you better at everything else.

131
00:06:01,932 --> 00:06:05,262
Under the regions, Leonida is split into counties,

132
00:06:05,262 --> 00:06:08,592
mostly identified from road signs, police cars and

133
00:06:08,592 --> 00:06:11,921
sheriff branding. Vice-Dale in the south east holds

134
00:06:11,921 --> 00:06:15,251
Vice City, Vice Beach, Ocean Beach, the port

135
00:06:15,251 --> 00:06:16,500
and the airport.

136
00:06:16,750 --> 00:06:19,769
Leonard County in the north east includes Waning

137
00:06:19,769 --> 00:06:22,787
Sands. Kelly County in the north west holds

138
00:06:22,787 --> 00:06:25,806
Port Gellhorn. And Mariana County in the south

139
00:06:25,806 --> 00:06:28,825
west covers the Grassrivers, the Keys, Key Lento,

140
00:06:28,825 --> 00:06:30,334
Watson Bay and Capri.

141
00:06:30,584 --> 00:06:34,956
Leonida is alive. An in-game chart lists alligators,

142
00:06:34,956 --> 00:06:39,327
boars, dogs, snakes, raccoons, birds, frogs, bobcats and

143
00:06:39,327 --> 00:06:43,699
rodents, with separate symbols for plants and even

144
00:06:43,699 --> 00:06:44,792
toxic waste.

145
00:06:45,042 --> 00:06:47,851
Add Mount Kalaga's deer, cougars and foxes, plus

146
00:06:47,851 --> 00:06:50,659
flamingos in the wetlands, and it's the most

147
00:06:50,659 --> 00:06:53,468
varied wildlife of any GTA. Some of it

148
00:06:53,468 --> 00:06:56,277
is beautiful, and some of it will absolutely

149
00:06:56,277 --> 00:06:57,330
ruin your day.

150
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:59,908
Watch for animal tracks too. In Focus Mode

151
00:06:59,908 --> 00:07:02,236
you can follow them, which is how you'll

152
00:07:02,236 --> 00:07:04,564
find the better hunting spots in the north.

153
00:07:04,814 --> 00:07:07,647
With a map this big, travel matters. There's

154
00:07:07,647 --> 00:07:10,481
no warping from the map. You use the

155
00:07:10,481 --> 00:07:13,314
RydeMe app, buses and trains on schedules, or

156
00:07:13,314 --> 00:07:16,148
switch characters, and the trains cover the whole

157
00:07:16,148 --> 00:07:16,502
region.

158
00:07:16,752 --> 00:07:19,368
RydeMe will even get you there instantly for

159
00:07:19,368 --> 00:07:21,984
an extra hundred dollars. But honestly, with a

160
00:07:21,984 --> 00:07:24,600
world this detailed, driving is half the fun.

161
00:07:24,850 --> 00:07:27,408
And the fastest trick of all is switching

162
00:07:27,408 --> 00:07:29,966
characters. The one you're not using usually waits

163
00:07:29,966 --> 00:07:32,524
near your current safehouse, so a switch can

164
00:07:32,524 --> 00:07:34,762
move you across the map in seconds.

165
00:07:35,012 --> 00:07:38,420
Now, what's not confirmed. Lummox County in the

166
00:07:38,420 --> 00:07:41,828
north only appears in leaked material, not official

167
00:07:41,828 --> 00:07:45,236
releases. And mapping projects disagree on exactly where

168
00:07:45,236 --> 00:07:46,940
Leonard and Ambrosia sit.

169
00:07:47,190 --> 00:07:49,833
A full map leaked in August reportedly came

170
00:07:49,833 --> 00:07:52,477
from an older internal build, so its borders

171
00:07:52,477 --> 00:07:55,120
and town names may not match the final

172
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:57,763
game. And Gloriana, once rumoured to be a

173
00:07:57,763 --> 00:08:00,407
whole separate state, looks like it's just a

174
00:08:00,407 --> 00:08:01,398
single key island.

175
00:08:01,648 --> 00:08:04,720
Several other place names have surfaced too, like

176
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:07,792
Crosstown, Rockridge and Catalan Key, but their source

177
00:08:07,792 --> 00:08:10,864
isn't clear, so treat them as rumours until

178
00:08:10,864 --> 00:08:12,400
you find them yourself.

179
00:08:12,650 --> 00:08:15,393
Before the recap, my personal ranking. Number one

180
00:08:15,393 --> 00:08:18,136
is Vice City at night. The neon strip,

181
00:08:18,136 --> 00:08:20,879
the nightlife and the sheer density of things

182
00:08:20,879 --> 00:08:23,621
to walk into make it the best city

183
00:08:23,621 --> 00:08:24,650
Rockstar has built.

184
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:27,532
Number two is the Grassrivers. Nothing else in

185
00:08:27,532 --> 00:08:30,165
GTA feels like gliding through a flooded swamp

186
00:08:30,165 --> 00:08:32,797
on an airboat with alligators around you. And

187
00:08:32,797 --> 00:08:35,430
number three is Mount Kalaga, for when you

188
00:08:35,430 --> 00:08:37,404
want the game to slow down.

189
00:08:37,654 --> 00:08:40,406
The underrated pick is Port Gellhorn. It looks

190
00:08:40,406 --> 00:08:43,158
forgotten on purpose, and that's exactly what makes

191
00:08:43,158 --> 00:08:45,910
it feel real. Don't skip it just because

192
00:08:45,910 --> 00:08:46,942
it isn't shiny.

193
00:08:47,192 --> 00:08:49,709
And if you want the most out of

194
00:08:49,709 --> 00:08:52,225
the map, slow down. With this many interiors,

195
00:08:52,225 --> 00:08:54,742
the best stuff is inside buildings, not on

196
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:56,000
the roads between them.

197
00:08:56,250 --> 00:08:58,699
So where should you go first? Do the

198
00:08:58,699 --> 00:09:01,149
Keys content early, explore Vice City at night

199
00:09:01,149 --> 00:09:03,598
for the nightlife, take an airboat through the

200
00:09:03,598 --> 00:09:06,047
Grassrivers, and save Mount Kalaga for when you

201
00:09:06,047 --> 00:09:07,578
want a break from crime.

202
00:09:07,828 --> 00:09:11,820
Quick recap. Six regions: Vice City, the Leonida

203
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:15,813
Keys, the Grassrivers, Port Gellhorn, Ambrosia and Mount

204
00:09:15,813 --> 00:09:19,805
Kalaga. Five counties. Over seven hundred interiors. And

205
00:09:19,805 --> 00:09:23,798
a landmass nearly as big as three Rockstar

206
00:09:23,798 --> 00:09:24,796
games combined.

207
00:09:25,046 --> 00:09:28,235
Which region are you exploring first? Tell me

208
00:09:28,235 --> 00:09:31,424
in the comments, and subscribe, because next we're

209
00:09:31,424 --> 00:09:34,214
meeting the characters of GTA 6, spoiler-free.
